WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.378 --> 00:00:01.807
- I have one job.

00:00:01.807 --> 00:00:05.198
Making the best clothing in the world.

00:00:05.198 --> 00:00:07.781
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.207 --> 00:00:12.338
My name is Martin Greenfield.

00:00:12.338 --> 00:00:16.628
I used to be Maxmilian
Grunfeld when I was born.

00:00:16.628 --> 00:00:19.528
But I changed it to make it American.

00:00:19.528 --> 00:00:22.595
Because I love this country.

00:00:22.595 --> 00:00:25.884
My craft is very difficult to define

00:00:25.884 --> 00:00:28.158
because it's many things.

00:00:28.158 --> 00:00:29.971
I am a maker of clothing.

00:00:29.971 --> 00:00:31.804
I know how to measure.

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:34.819
I know how to fit people.

00:00:34.819 --> 00:00:38.013
Very few people could match me.

00:00:38.013 --> 00:00:40.901
I was responsible for all the Presidents.

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:43.505
Clinton, I measured in the White House.

00:00:43.505 --> 00:00:45.259
Obama, measured in the White House.

00:00:45.259 --> 00:00:47.437
So then I made them perfect suits.

00:00:47.437 --> 00:00:50.353
We never had to fix nothing.

00:00:50.353 --> 00:00:52.853
(loudspeaker)

00:00:55.451 --> 00:00:59.077
My life was a sad life
before I came to America

00:00:59.077 --> 00:01:01.018
because I lost my family.

00:01:01.018 --> 00:01:03.942
I was left alone, everybody was dead.

00:01:03.942 --> 00:01:05.508
We were occupied,

00:01:05.508 --> 00:01:07.715
Auschwitz was a month later.

00:01:07.715 --> 00:01:12.293
I was in the concentration
camp a year and two months.

00:01:12.293 --> 00:01:14.578
It was my second day in Auschwitz,

00:01:14.578 --> 00:01:18.014
there was no more names
at the concentration camp,

00:01:18.014 --> 00:01:19.097
only numbers.

00:01:20.322 --> 00:01:21.877
When they called me,

00:01:21.877 --> 00:01:23.678
they sent me to a tailor.

00:01:23.678 --> 00:01:26.155
The head tailor spoke my language,

00:01:26.155 --> 00:01:27.148
he was Jewish.

00:01:27.148 --> 00:01:28.925
They asked me, "Are you a tailor?"

00:01:28.925 --> 00:01:30.085
No.

00:01:30.085 --> 00:01:33.266
I said if you could show
me how to make the collar.

00:01:33.266 --> 00:01:35.202
He says, "I'll make you a collar."

00:01:35.202 --> 00:01:37.971
Showed me how to make a collar.

00:01:37.971 --> 00:01:42.261
The pain is still in my
heart about my family.

00:01:42.261 --> 00:01:46.236
I still dream about my
family like they're alive.

00:01:46.236 --> 00:01:49.486
But on the outside you will never know.

00:01:50.971 --> 00:01:53.831
I didn't think I was gonna survive.

00:01:53.831 --> 00:01:56.331
I was liberated by Eisenhower.

00:01:57.338 --> 00:02:01.505
General Eisenhower came in
when I was 15 1/2 years old

00:02:02.538 --> 00:02:03.744
and when they walked in,

00:02:03.744 --> 00:02:07.494
I shook his hand crying,
"You saved my life".

00:02:09.307 --> 00:02:12.640
I came to America, September 18th, 1947.

00:02:15.575 --> 00:02:17.992
They gave me the job as a tailor.

00:02:17.992 --> 00:02:19.282
I told my boss,

00:02:19.282 --> 00:02:22.706
"Listen, Eisenhower liberated me.

00:02:22.706 --> 00:02:25.993
"I want you to make him a three-piece suit

00:02:25.993 --> 00:02:27.532
"like I wear myself."

00:02:27.532 --> 00:02:28.875
He like it.

00:02:28.875 --> 00:02:31.105
Once he had the first three-piece suit

00:02:31.105 --> 00:02:32.989
from then on you didn't see Eisenhower

00:02:32.989 --> 00:02:35.114
in nothing but three-piece suits.

00:02:35.114 --> 00:02:36.652
So that's how it started.

00:02:36.652 --> 00:02:40.152
I made sure we dressed all the Presidents.

00:02:41.124 --> 00:02:44.327
With Obama, first he
wanted me to copy a suit.

00:02:44.327 --> 00:02:45.731
I don't copy anybody.

00:02:45.731 --> 00:02:47.755
Everybody copies my suits.

00:02:47.755 --> 00:02:50.527
So, if he wants me to make something

00:02:50.527 --> 00:02:52.476
I have to measure.

00:02:52.476 --> 00:02:54.380
Next day, he sends an e-mail

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:57.604
"It will be a pleasure to meet you there."

00:02:57.604 --> 00:03:00.084
I'm happy when I'm at the factory.

00:03:00.084 --> 00:03:04.350
My job is the most
important thing in my life.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.538
Quality is so important to me

00:03:06.538 --> 00:03:10.290
because I know that's
what kept me in business

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.583
and that's why I'm here talking to you.

00:03:12.583 --> 00:03:15.166
(upbeat music)

